meta {
  name: 01 - Multi-Tool Reasoning (FAQ + Balance in One Message)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/api/agent/chat
  body: json
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {
    "conversationId": "agent-test-1",
    "accountId": "ACC1001",
    "message": "What is the penalty for early FD withdrawal, and also what is my current balance?"
  }
}

docs {
  THE flagship test for this endpoint. This is the concrete proof of the
  difference between /api/agent/chat and the Step 4 router
  (/api/assistant/chat): a single message that needs BOTH the FAQ agent
  and the banking-actions agent to be fully answered.

  Run the identical message through 05-orchestrator's requests against
  /api/assistant/chat for direct comparison — the router can only ever
  pick ONE of FAQ or BANKING, never both.

  To verify this worked (not just that a plausible-sounding answer came
  back), watch the Spring Boot application console while this request
  runs. You should see BOTH of these log lines appear:
    [Agent] answerBankingFaq called: ...
    [Agent] performBankingAction called: ...
  If only one appears, the model chose not to call both tools for this
  phrasing - worth noting, not necessarily a bug, but not the intended
  demonstration either.
}
